{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X3G6Qwq8x4maV5N3bMgNXR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've successfully read the file. Here are the requirements you requested:\n\n## R2.15\n**Text:** -i and -s may be combined. When both are given, inode is printed first, then block count, then the entry (or the long-format fields).\n\n**Line:** 126-127\n\n---\n\n## R3.1\n**Text:** Must support --color=always, --color=auto, and --color=never. When --color is given without a value, it must default to \"always\".\n\n**Line:** 132-133\n\n---\n\n## R3.2\n**Text:** --color=auto must colorize output only when stdout is a TTY. TTY detection: call pkg/sys.IsTerminal(os.Stdout) — returns true when os.Stdout's file descriptor is a terminal (detected via golang.org/x/sys/unix.IoctlGetWinsize with TIOCGWINSZ), false otherwise. When stdout is not a TTY, --color=auto must behave like --color=never.\n\n**Line:** 134-136\n\n---\n\n## R3.3\n**Text:** Colorized output uses GNU LS_COLORS default color assignments via pkg/format. Call pkg/format.FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string to obtain the ANSI escape sequence for a given file type, and pkg/format.Reset() string for the reset sequence. Executable detection: fi.Mode&0o111 != 0 (any execute bit set). Each entry name is wrapped as: colorCode + name + resetCode. When color is suppressed, both codes are empty strings so no ANSI sequences appear in output.\n\nSet the process-global color mode based on the --color flag value: call pkg/format.SetColorEnabled(true) for --color=always, pkg/format.SetColorEnabled(false) for --color=never. For --color=auto, call pkg/sys.IsTerminal(os.Stdout.Fd()) and pass the result to pkg/format.SetColorEnabled. When color is disabled, pkg/format.FileTypeColor returns empty strings.\n\n**Line:** 137-141"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6949b217-412c-4560-bd4a-9e3e6a1dfd95","uuid":"5c34cb82-7468-4bc5-87f4-673c3b8ef128","timestamp":"2026-05-14T2